  "question": {
    "text": "For ac circuit shown in figure, $\\mathrm{R}=100 \\mathrm{k} \\Omega$ and $\\mathrm{C}=100 \\mathrm{pF}$ and the phase difference between $\\mathrm{V}_{\\text {in }}$ and $\\left(V_B-V_A\\right)$ is $90^{\\circ}$. The input signal frequency is $10^x \\mathrm{rad} / \\mathrm{sec}$, where ' x ' is ______<br/><img src=\"assets\\qt0001_e6718c0cfea5.png\"/>"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "5",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<img src=\"assets\\st0001_489aa3e09a55.png\"/><br/>$\\theta+\\theta=90^{\\circ} ; \\theta=45^{\\circ}$<br/>$\\tan \\theta=\\frac{\\mathrm{X}_{\\mathrm{C}}}{\\mathrm{R}}$<br/>$\\mathrm{X}_{\\mathrm{C}}=\\mathrm{R} \\Rightarrow \\frac{1}{\\mathrm{~W}_{\\mathrm{C}}}=\\mathrm{R}$<br/>$\\mathrm{W}=\\frac{1}{\\mathrm{R}_{\\mathrm{C}}}=\\frac{1}{100 \\times 10^3 \\times 100 \\times 10^{-12}}$<br/>$=\\frac{10^{12}}{10^7}=10^5$"
  }
}